# A turn of a typed copy may begin again in the closed copy only while it has done nothing that can be seen. Here a variable of the file is stored in front of the pattern: the value is not held there, and the turn of the third row,
# which has an iterator of its own, counts once.
# THE LIE, testing=TurnsAreTakenToHaveDoneNothingWherePatternsAreHeld: the hold is laid though the turn has stored. The turn of the third row begins again behind its store and counts twice.
